# Veridian runtime state — filesystem-first, portable, never committed.
.veridian/

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
*.tgz

# The build output. Generated by `npm run build`, never edited, and reproduced from the source tree
# on any machine - so committing it would be committing a copy that can silently disagree with the
# source it was compiled from. `npm pack` and `npm publish` run `prepare` and rebuild it.
dist/

# Playwright artifacts that escape the run bundle
test-results/
playwright-report/

# The database the `inventory-db` example builds. Like `.veridian/`, it is a world this machine
# produced, not source: it is deleted and rebuilt from `app/build.mjs` on every start and every reset,
# so committing it would commit a copy that can disagree with the script that makes it. The demo's
# restore does not need to remove it - the build removes it, which is what makes a reset a reset.
examples/inventory-db/app/**.db

# The substitute image registry the `sim-k8s` example's build produces. Same reasoning as the database
# above, and one consequence on top of it: this directory is what the world's control plane reads to
# decide whether an image can be pulled, so committing it would let a manifest naming a tag the build
# never produced pull successfully - a false PASS in the world's own evidence, kept in the repository.
examples/sim-k8s/app/build/

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
